3. Data

   Both data sets are bundled into the app and loaded only on a screen where
   someone sets a password. Nothing is fetched at run time. How they were made
   is documented in src/client/lib/password/data/SOURCES.md.

   a. Common-password blocklist
      (src/client/lib/password/data/common-roots.txt and common-long.txt)
      Cut from the SecLists file
      Passwords/Common-Credentials/xato-net-10-million-passwords-1000000.txt
      (https://github.com/danielmiessler/SecLists).
      Licence of SecLists: MIT, Copyright (c) 2018 Daniel Miessler.
      Origin of the data: Mark Burnett's 2015 "ten million passwords" data set,
      which he released to the public domain. His request, honoured here, is that
      the data is used for research and for making authentication more secure;
      this app uses it only to refuse weak passwords.

   b. Passphrase word list (src/client/lib/password/data/wordlist.txt)
      The English word list of BIP-39 (bip-0039/english.txt in
      https://github.com/bitcoin/bips), unchanged. Licence: MIT ("This BIP falls
      under the MIT License"). Authors: Marek Palatinus, Pavol Rusnak, Aaron
      Voisine, Sean Bowe.

   c. Test vectors (test/crypto/)
      cfrg-p256.json is one HPKE test vector (mode 0, DHKEM(P-256, HKDF-SHA256),
      HKDF-SHA256, AES-256-GCM) from the interoperability test-vector set that
      the IETF CFRG publishes for RFC 9180
      (https://github.com/cfrg/draft-irtf-cfrg-hpke). The file states no
      licence of its own; it is a published test value, used only by the tests
      and not shipped. vectors.json and vectors-v4.json are known-answer vectors
      written for this project.


4. Fonts

   No font file is shipped in this repository or in the build. index.html asks
   the visitor's browser to load Geist and Geist Mono from Google Fonts at run
   time (the browser contacts Google when the app opens). Geist is published by
   Vercel under the SIL Open Font License 1.1
   (https://github.com/vercel/geist-font). Self-hosting the font files, or
   removing the request, is listed in docs/security.md under known limitations.


